+      "basis": "studies/simulation-validity/README.md, Desk research A, row 'What error is normal': a plus or minus 35 percent interval proposed in the literature as a standard of model adequacy (quoted from a search summary, the paper was not read). A grid should not use up the whole adequacy band by itself, so this mark asks only that the coarse grids sit inside it."
+    },
+    "fuzz": {
+      "claim": "Random terrains, weather and ignitions, extremes included, never give a NaN, a negative or impossible area, runaway growth or a burnt cell that un-burns.",
+      "setup": "Forty seeded cases (seeds 1001 to 1040) in the default run and a longer sweep in the background; each case draws a domain of 900 to 3000 m with a cell of 20, 30 or 40 m, a terrain of seeded hills and a plane (0 to about 60 degrees locally), fuel type, wind 0 to 120 km/h, temperature minus 5 to 48 C, relative humidity 2 to 100 percent, cloud, drought factor 0 to 10, one to three ignitions (points, lines, at the edge and at the corner, some starting later than 0), embers on or off, fast tier (the standard tier under SLOW on a smaller domain), 20 to 60 minutes.",
+      "mark": "In every snapshot: no NaN anywhere in the fire, moisture, wind-felt and embers arrays or in the stats (an unburnt cell's arrival time is Infinity, which is allowed); burnt area at least 0 and at most the domain's area; burnt area never decreases; the arrival time of a cell never changes once set and a burnt cell stays burnt; the head rate of spread never exceeds the level-set cap; with embers off no cell is reached sooner than its distance from the nearest ignition divided by the cap, to within two cells; time never goes back.",
+      "capSource": "SPREAD_PARAMS.levelSet.rosMaxMs in src/fire/spread/params.ts"
