Subject: [PATCH 2/6] 0.10.0 validity: metamorphic properties, convergence
 bands and the stress fuzz, with their findings

Properties over seeded random terrains: a quarter turn turns the result (to 0.01 s measured, not bit for bit), more wind never slows the head, more moisture never speeds it, a firebreak never raises the burnt area, a later change leaves earlier snapshots unchanged (from the start and by rewind). Grid and step refinement against stated bands on synthetic terrain and on Katoomba and the Warrumbungles. Fuzz of random terrains, weather and ignitions. Findings, reported and not fixed: F1 (the Head fire figure above the 6 m/s cap, pinned) and F2 (one 2 s step 10.4 percent off, pinned). The pass-mark revisions are recorded in passMarks.json.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

