+# 1986 Annaburroo grass fires: can the data be had? (idea 11 of plan 15d)
+
+**Status.** Reached once, on 2026-11-08, from the build sandbox (a restricted proxy): the dataset's public **metadata record** was read. **The data
+files were not downloaded, nothing was run, and no number from them is in this repository.** The orchestrator decides whether to use it.
+
+**What was read.** `https://doi.org/10.25919/ycd3-w209` (the DOI named in the desk research) redirected to the CSIRO Data Access Portal collection
+`https://data.csiro.au/collection/csiro:58746`, and the portal's own metadata service (`https://data.csiro.au/dap/ws/v2/collections/58746`, answered
+HTTP 200 with JSON) gave the record kept in [`record.json`](record.json) as received (re-indented only). The facts that matter, from that record:
+
+| Field | Value (as the record says) |
+|---|---|
+| Title | 1986 Annaburroo Experimental Grassland Fire Data |
+| Licence | Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International Licence (`licenceLink` `https://data.csiro.au/dap/ws/v2/licences/1121`) |
+| Access | "The metadata and files (if any) are available to the public." `accessLevel` Public, `dataRestricted` FALSE |
+| Files | `fileCount` 2 (the files were not listed or fetched) |
+| Attribution | Gould, Jim; Gomes Da Cruz, Miguel; & Sullivan, Andrew (2023): 1986 Annaburroo Experimental Grassland Fire Data. v1. CSIRO. Data Collection. https://data.csiro.au/collection/csiro:58746 |
+| What it holds | 121 experimental fires in grass at Annaburroo Station (Northern Territory): fuel, weather and fire behaviour measurements used to develop the CSIRO Grassland Fire Spread Model (1998) |
+| Contact | Andrew Sullivan, CSIRO |
+
+**What this means.** The data are public and the licence permits use with attribution, so a grass rate-of-spread test against real fires (the cheapest
+comparison with real fire behaviour, `../README.md` Desk research B2) looks possible. What is **not** known: what the two files contain and in what format,
+how their wind, moisture and fuel columns map onto FireSim's inputs, and how FireSim's grass model (spec section 6.5) would be set up for plots of 100 to 300 m.
+Per the contract the work stops here. It stays in the claims register as a known gap (`C-ANNABURROO`, `src/sim/validation/claims.json`).
+
+## The other two sources named by the contract (hindcasts, a peer model), looked at once each, 2026-11-08
+
+- **Recorded-fire perimeters (idea 13).** One request for the NSW Fire History record on the state data portal
+  (`https://data.nsw.gov.au/data/api/3/action/package_show?id=fa2fe6c7-2530-4b5a-87dc-5afdb290141a`, the dataset the desk research named) answered **HTTP 403, "Access denied:
+  User not authorized to read package"**. Not reached: its licence and whether the Gospers Mountain 2019 perimeter is in it are still unchecked. No hindcast was made.
+- **A peer model (idea 18).** One request for the ELMFIRE repository's public record through the GitHub API (`https://api.github.com/repos/lautenberger/elmfire`; the name is from
+  memory) answered **HTTP 403, "GitHub access to this repository is not enabled for this session"**. Not reached, and nothing was installed or run. A peer comparison also needs
+  fuel classes mapped by hand and a second program to be run, so it needs more than a dataset.
+
+Both are recorded in the register as known gaps (`C-HINDCAST-PEER`). Nothing was typed in from memory.
+
+If the Annaburroo data are used later: record the licence and attribution in `public/demo/provenance.json`-style provenance for the study, pin the file versions, write the pass
+mark first (the literature figure of about 21 percent error for grass models is from a search summary and was not read), and compare statistics over the
+experiments, not one fire.
