+# Claims register
+
+<!-- Generated by scripts/validity-card.mjs from src/sim/validation/claims.json. Do not edit by hand: edit the JSON and run the script. -->
+
+The claims register of FireSim (plan 15d, idea 2; contract 0.10.0, 4.3 item 4): every number and behaviour the app shows a person, with where it is shown, its source, what the check compares it with, the check (a test: file and title), the pass mark, its known error and its status. docs/validity/claims.md and the card in 'How sure are we?' (card.json) are both made from this file and the measured results by scripts/validity-card.mjs. claims.test.ts fails when a check named here does not exist, when a status says more than its checks allow, or when the card or the page is out of date. Text in double braces is replaced with a figure read from a file (run, conv, tiers, golden); nothing else in a known error is a measured figure of this release.
+
+**Scope.** In: the model card (How this simulation works, all seven sections), the Head fire and other statistics tiles, the insight cards by kind, the Help glossary's numbers, the wind and air displays' statements about what they show, the cliff drawing's statement about the numbers. Out for now (not yet listed): the Setup screen's wording, the Data sets screen's statements of provenance (partly held by truthAudit.test.ts and the scenario dataset tests), the colours and legends.
+
+**58 claims:** 14 checked, 33 partly, 2 unchecked, 9 known gaps. **Nothing in this register has been compared with a recorded fire.** Every "checked" is a check against a formula, a published rule of thumb or a property; `comparedWith` says which.
+
+## What the statuses mean
+
+- **checked**: A test compares the number or behaviour with its source (a formula, a published rule of thumb, an exact property) and passes. It says nothing about real fires unless 'comparedWith' says so.
+- **partly**: A test covers part of the claim (one tier, one range, one case) or its form only, or the source itself is partly unverified. A measurement stored in a file counts as a check here when it is named under measurements; it is not a test that re-runs.
+- **unchecked**: No test covers it.
+- **known gap**: A check or a measurement shows the claim does not hold in some case, or the app already admits it is uncalibrated or unreviewed.
+
